                                "sense_id": "df6e73da-d65f-3122-b058-7418fb82c46c",
                                "text": "She had her knees up, resting her wrists on them; the pepperbox muzzle of a flechette pistol emerged from her hands."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1e14276-df0e-3ddc-a3df-c4158d636f43",
                        "entry_id": "3a72688a-d623-3a81-aa64-d434df8b9948",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A buttress at one side of the court in the game of fives."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ce25987-1a94-36ee-a473-207ed66a0d48",
                        "entry_id": "3a72688a-d623-3a81-aa64-d434df8b9948",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tower capped by a cupola, looking similar to a giant pepper shaker."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7575767b-2202-49bc-b604-9063ddf8902b",
                                "sense_id": "7ce25987-1a94-36ee-a473-207ed66a0d48",
                                "text": "Large, stately, and dark was its [the château's] outline against the dusky night-sky; there were pepper-boxes and tourelles and what-not fantastically going up into the dim starlight."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00803355-76ed-3d62-8569-e9d02dc9ca12",
                        "entry_id": "3a72688a-d623-3a81-aa64-d434df8b9948",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of the buildings of the Royal Academy and National Gallery in Trafalgar Square, London, having cupolas on the roof."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "in-plural",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "084900a8-208b-4fb9-9aba-08cb9b377fc9",
                                "sense_id": "00803355-76ed-3d62-8569-e9d02dc9ca12",
                                "text": "I also remember the old Royal Mews that stood on the site of the present trumpery National Gallery, with its too suggestive pepper-boxes; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66aa87fd-3b85-4014-8f62-9cd2822c9d3f",
                                "sense_id": "00803355-76ed-3d62-8569-e9d02dc9ca12",
                                "text": "Its architect, Wilkins, had the misfortune to be chosen to erect our much-abused National Gallery building, with its condemned \"pepper-boxes\" of cupolas; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
